tau is cyclic (dL/dtau = 0): True
first integral p_tau = mu_K**2*(-N(t) + Derivative(tau(t), t))*a(t)**3/(K*N(t))  -> a^3 mu^2 (Q-1)/K = C, C unconstrained
rho_K(Q) = mu_K**2*(q - 1)*(q + 1)/(2*K)  (record: mu^2(Q^2-1)/2K)
on shell rho_K = C**2*K/(2*mu_K**2*a(t)**6) + C/a(t)**3
Friedmann: Eq(3*H**2/(2*K), C**2*K/(2*mu_K**2*a(t)**6) + C/a(t)**3 + rho_b0/a(t)**3 + Lambda/(2*K))
Solve Friedmann for C (it only trades C for H): [mu_K*(-mu_K*a(t)**3 - sqrt((3*H**2*a(t)**3 - 2*K*rho_b0 - Lambda*a(t)**3 + mu_K**2*a(t)**3)*a(t)**3))/K]
late R = C/rho_b0
Pi - D_iP^i = 0
sqrt(h)*(1/Q)div[(1+gPi)P] - d_i(N sqrt h (1+gPi)P^i) = 0
eps*J_B.dtau term in minisuperspace = eps*n_B0*Derivative(tau(t), t) -> d/dt(eps n_B0 tau): total derivative, E3 unchanged
